{
  "comment": [
    "Families pair gofhir diagnostic IDs with HL7 validator message IDs that report the same finding.",
    "A gofhir error and an HL7 error can be matched only within one family, and only where the family's",
    "location rule holds: 'equal' (same normalized location) or 'parent' (same location, or one is the",
    "immediate parent of the other; HL7 reports a missing child at its parent and a required slice at the",
    "owner of the list). FHIRPath constraints are matched by constraint key, at the equal location.",
    "hl7 entries are exact IDs, or prefixes when they end in '*'. hl7NoID matches HL7 issues that carry no",
    "message ID, by issue code and a regular expression on the text.",
    "Every gofhir ID in pkg/issue is either in a family or listed under 'unmapped' with a reason; a test",
    "enforces it. Unmapped and family-less errors never match: they always count as unexplained on their",
    "side, so a change in them is always visible.",
    "Rules are 'parent' only where the corpus shows HL7 reporting at the parent (cardinality, slicing, unknown elements, extension value types) and the finding is named or located precisely enough; everything else is 'equal', which can only make a pair less likely, never a wrong one.",
    "quotesElement marks families whose gofhir messages quote the element they are about ('Minimum cardinality of 'X:slice.y''); the slices of that element are part of the error's identity and are compared with HL7's.",
    "An ID may be in several families. HL7's 'Slice ... a matching slice is required' (_SLICE) is a required slice and pairs only with gofhir's slice cardinality error, never with an element minimum; HL7's element minimum ('X: minimum required') pairs with either."
  ],
  "families": [
    {
      "name": "cardinality-min",
      "rule": "parent",
      "gofhir": [
        "CARDINALITY_MIN",
        "SLICING_CARDINALITY_MIN"
      ],
      "hl7": [
        "Validation_VAL_Profile_Minimum"
      ],
      "quotesElement": true
    },
    {
      "name": "slice-required",
      "rule": "parent",
      "quotesElement": true,
      "gofhir": [
        "SLICING_CARDINALITY_MIN"
      ],
      "hl7": [
        "Validation_VAL_Profile_Minimum_SLICE",
        "Validation_VAL_Profile_Minimum_SLICE_EXT"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "cardinality-max",
      "rule": "parent",
      "gofhir": [
        "CARDINALITY_MAX",
        "SLICING_CARDINALITY_MAX"
      ],
      "hl7": [
        "Validation_VAL_Profile_Maximum"
      ],
      "quotesElement": true
    },
    {
      "name": "extension-value-required",
      "rule": "equal",
      "gofhir": [
        "EXTENSION_VALUE_REQUIRED"
      ],
      "hl7": [
        "Extension_EXT_Simple_ABSENT"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "slice-no-match",
      "rule": "equal",
      "gofhir": [
        "SLICING_NO_MATCH"
      ],
      "hl7": [
        "Validation_VAL_Profile_NotSlice"
